 companies. This is the first known instance of Google's AI systems engaging in such behavior autonomously.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Trump signs broad Russia sanctions bill</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d51d86ba8d85a1ce8c9a92cd8e4b02811d98f9aa424face8a3a759453e5f1fb7</id><updated>2026-09-19T04:47:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T01:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-signs-broad-russia-sanctions-bill/a-79335115--6fedb45cc326.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-signs-broad-russia-sanctions-bill/a-79335115?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The bill signed by US President Donald Trump targets officials, banks, and a fleet of shadow tankers that transport Russian energy.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Deal with Denmark gives US 'permanent control' over Greenland security, Trump says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94f59008661983465b044d76cd333598d1ed03fc81ccc26bb8b73a1da16860d3</id><updated>2026-09-19T04:47:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T21:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/deal-with-denmark-gives-us-permanent-control-over-greenland-security-trump-says/a-79334915--f1981ff32b95.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/deal-with-denmark-gives-us-permanent-control-over-greenland-security-trump-says/a-79334915?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The deal with Denmark, according to President Donald Trump, would give the US "permanent control" over Greenland's security. Denmark said the deal is "great for NATO and Europe."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Trump bars CNN, MS NOW and Politico from White House</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e1014be03842ec5da26ea2cdf1e039a87e551c534ea3e272f40803bd21abcf42</id><updated>2026-09-19T04:47:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T20:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-bars-cnn-ms-now-and-politico-from-white-house/a-79334846--33e55a60f5f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-bars-cnn-ms-now-and-politico-from-white-house/a-79334846?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump has accused CNN, MS NOW and Politico of spreading fake news. The outlets have vowed to take legal action against the ban.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran's 'new Hezbollah:' How powerful are the Houthis now?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1665009930da26f85351df7cafe3c02ced9d0e59ab28c56ad443a36efedbb241</id><updated>2026-09-19T04:47:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T19:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-s-new-hezbollah-how-powerful-are-the-houthis-now/a-79331945--4b9ea7a40292.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-s-new-hezbollah-how-powerful-are-the-houthis-now/a-79331945?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After Houthi victories in Yemen, the group's importance in the US-Iran war has grown. Previously Lebanon's Hezbollah was considered most significant in Iran's "axis of resistance." Now the Houthis are rising to the top.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ryanair boss apologizes for calling other airlines 'rapists'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9b164b3872a161b38796d9b7f3b6af48adb2cb7787ec8a876ae56c7303cbd4f7</id><updated>2026-09-19T04:47:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T19:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ryanair-boss-apologizes-for-calling-other-airlines-rapists/a-79334099--f47b48dc904d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ryanair-boss-apologizes-for-calling-other-airlines-rapists/a-79334099?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The airline CEO had used the term to describe other airlines with high fares. His comments were criticized by officials both in Ireland and the UK.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Strait of Hormuz attacks spill oil into Persian Gulf</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ba11ee74531b51663d2823cb5e55d5b2634753de497cc2170699bc366d2c981</id><updated>2026-09-19T04:46:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T19:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/strait-of-hormuz-attacks-spill-oil-into-persian-gulf/a-79327092--09836173253c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/strait-of-hormuz-attacks-spill-oil-into-persian-gulf/a-79327092?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As war disrupts one of the world's busiest shipping lanes, satellite images reveal that oil is spreading toward protected coral reefs and mangrove forests.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Ebola: DR Congo outbreak not slowing, MSF warns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c24b75fb7f25fbad931d91946d42081b3717d3f3cf2422de067ebab8bc453259</id><updated>2026-09-19T04:46:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T18:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ebola-dr-congo-outbreak-not-slowing-msf-warns/a-79333719--f40efdc02bf4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ebola-dr-congo-outbreak-not-slowing-msf-warns/a-79333719?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Doctors Without Borders has warned against premature optimism amid the DRC's largest-ever Ebola outbreak. "The outbreak is not shrinking, it is moving," an MSF official said, entering new and more underprepared regions.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Airport malaria in Germany remains infrequent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ff87cbc3d305fd524ba4610290fca89197b9a384ac643ce3b88f32c4a11066d3</id><updated>2026-09-19T04:46:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T18:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/airport-malaria-in-germany-remains-infrequent/a-79333920--b6e9f1b4961f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/airport-malaria-in-germany-remains-infrequent/a-79333920?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">An outbreak of malaria at Frankfurt Airport this summer has raised alarm. Experts believe parasites probably arrived in a passenger's luggage. But with the onset of fall, the risks of contracting the disease are low.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Fact Check: False video alleges Berlin votes destroyed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:952c251d35165e0896289ad1d9dda138b331aa083aaa4e40bf55ac06664465d5</id><updated>2026-09-19T04:46:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T18:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-false-video-alleges-berlin-votes-destroyed/a-79333344--411939a21d7f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-false-video-alleges-berlin-votes-destroyed/a-79333344?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A video claiming to show AfD postal ballots being destroyed has gone viral ahead of Berlin's September 20 election. DW Fact Check examines the footage, the accounts sharing it and how widely it is really being viewed.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Zelenskyy holds inaugural 'Carpathian Eight' regional summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c51698cc16b6495b62a0c11faffb1a31fa6b75870b9d39b2c5cfa18d32dfa950</id><updated>2026-09-19T04:46:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T17:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/zelenskyy-holds-inaugural-carpathian-eight-regional-summit/a-79333437--f5a836e47847.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/zelenskyy-holds-inaugural-carpathian-eight-regional-summit/a-79333437?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Zelenskyy said the summit was a "significant beginning" of a movement to strengthen ties with its neighboring countries.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German police probe arson attack on Wuppertal synagogue</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c8f994cd7354a7d03dd4db8b6e74a37c25e29f48483c6c92288e67a70bd4cc11</id><updated>2026-09-19T04:46:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T15:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-police-probe-arson-attack-on-wuppertal-synagogue/a-79331270--dce70b32746f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-police-probe-arson-attack-on-wuppertal-synagogue/a-79331270?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The man detained shortly after allegedly trying to set fire to Wuppertal's synagogue made antisemitic comments to the arresting officers, prosecutors say. The 37-year-old Afghan citizen also had knives in his apartment.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Warren Buffett steps down as Berkshire Hathaway chairman</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:44b02f9bc0c7862c7fcb6625e59da52dc20540ff619e1d855391771c1427a3ea</id><updated>2026-09-19T04:46:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T15:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/warren-buffett-steps-down-as-berkshire-hathaway-chairman/a-79330594--2480bd95e8fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/warren-buffett-steps-down-as-berkshire-hathaway-chairman/a-79330594?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Buffett's son, Howard, will succeed him in the role. Buffett had earlier stepped down as Berkshire's CEO last year.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ever more Israelis moving to and investing in Cyprus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:19be0c02ffdae34c0b77a645432ee15319bfdb711f0708aba6bc77027a22ac20</id><updated>2026-09-19T04:46:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T15:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ever-more-israelis-moving-to-and-investing-in-cyprus/a-79330240--f9d83a8ed500.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ever-more-israelis-moving-to-and-investing-in-cyprus/a-79330240?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Over the past three years, more and more Israelis have been purchasing property and investing in Cyprus, with many moving to the island permanently. How has this changed the Cypriot economy and how are locals responding?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Canada and EU: A look at the bloc's special relationships</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9c0ad80a42566471d2859760cc4afb1c6968ea1e82862cb2afaa723de2d80dc</id><updated>2026-09-19T04:46:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T14:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/canada-and-eu-a-look-at-the-bloc-s-special-relationships/a-79328797--41616c65f5bb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/canada-and-eu-a-look-at-the-bloc-s-special-relationships/a-79328797?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Though Canada may be some distance from Europe geographically, closer political ties are in the cards. With talk of an associate membership, DW takes a look at other arrangements the EU has with particular countries.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Dual citizenship means Germany now in competition for talent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f6c8aa70cc3bd2ed61f70010172ba87b23bb595d11d4b6cf8b3ad8c393fc27f4</id><updated>2026-09-19T04:46:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T14:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dual-citizenship-means-germany-now-in-competition-for-talent/a-79330797--d43696518a30.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dual-citizenship-means-germany-now-in-competition-for-talent/a-79330797?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Coach Jürgen Klopp has named several players to his first Germany squad who are eligible to play for other countries. Some still aren't committed to playing for thje national team long-term.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>France: Macron orders defense against Russian hybrid attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a0e905a7d2b7c094fa7050f51f4617255760298aa34289f15e93abd7e34dffb7</id><updated>2026-09-19T04:46:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T13:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-macron-orders-defense-against-russian-hybrid-attacks/a-79329757--47108346e05e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-macron-orders-defense-against-russian-hybrid-attacks/a-79329757?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Emmanuel Macron said Russia's hybrid threat had "intensified" and called for plans to protect critical infrastructure.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Beethoven and Andy Warhol: Rebel icons on show in Bonn</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ea2179d9227ceb49dfe951b7cfefd7144752052d35f13d6148684b0fec37bb9</id><updated>2026-09-19T04:46:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T12:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/beethoven-and-andy-warhol-rebel-icons-on-show-in-bonn/a-79296944--59ad6d6535a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/beethoven-and-andy-warhol-rebel-icons-on-show-in-bonn/a-79296944?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The new exhibition "Beethoven by Warhol" at the Beethoven House in Bonn presents the pop artist's late masterpiece: a picture of Ludwig van Beethoven. The exhibition shares the story of the work with the public.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan suicide bombing targets police facility in Kohat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fbf7916424da87c2e6ee3c93f72b4e8b4c3d20d9b1189865a22379fa76c4d1d0</id><updated>2026-09-19T04:46:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T12:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-suicide-bombing-targets-police-facility-in-kohat/a-79327432--8b09a06dd711.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-suicide-bombing-targets-police-facility-in-kohat/a-79327432?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A police official said the explosion killed at least 16 people, injuring many more. The attacker targeted a police facility and damaged a mosque at the site. The president blamed the attack on the TTP Pakistani Taliban.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Is it possible to replace the chancellor?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8baf976eff7145b3e5ad9cb870949704258aa7c68713a5d4aea2b31804202315</id><updated>2026-09-19T04:47:23Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T12:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-is-it-possible-to-replace-the-chancellor/a-79313623--5363f1668974.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-is-it-possible-to-replace-the-chancellor/a-79313623?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz's record-low approval ratings have emboldened his opponents. There are three ways to remove a chancellor from office in Germany.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry></feed>
